pdated_at":"2022-07-05T21:41:20Z","body":"I did some more investigation. Apparently, the same thing happens with redux. The problem happens if I try to use the context/store in a component that is a direct child of `_app.jsx`, where the `Provider` is wrapping the application. If the target component is a child of the `Page` where I'm calling the function to update the context, it seems to work.\r\n\r\nMaybe Next.js evaluates the components tree from top to bottom during the SSR and doesn't go back to update things that were already rendered on the first render.\r\n\r\nThe other possibility is that react functions are ignoring for some reason the context/redux updates in parent components on the server-side when a child component is responsible for the update.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/1175526206/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"julianobrasil","id":25405143,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NDA1MTQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25405143?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianobrasil","html_url":"https://github.com/julianobrasil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianobrasil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianobrasil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianobrasil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianobrasil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianobrasil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianobrasil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianobrasil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianobrasil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/julianobrasil/received_events","type":"Us