mponents","hybrid","nextjs","node","react","server-rendering","ssg","static","static-site-generator","universal","vercel"],"visibility":"public","forks":30029,"open_issues":3156,"watchers":136480,"default_branch":"canary","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/pulls/39221","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/39221","diff_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/39221.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/pull/39221.patch","merged_at":"2022-08-01T14:21:42Z"},"body":"When we detect if `reactRoot` rendering should be enabled we `require` the require to check the version. But at that time the `NODE_ENV` isn't set yet. Then the react dev build stays in the `require.cache` that any future require of react will get the wrong build. In that case, React dev bundle is picked in production mode.\r\n\r\nFun fact: if you're using hooks, that seem not to effect you, but context consumer works different then you couldn't get the proper context from provider.\r\n\r\nFixes #38176\r\nFixes #38765\r\nFixes #38332\r\n\r\n## Bug\r\n\r\n- [x] Related issues linked using `fixes #number`\r\n- [ ] Integration tests added\r\n- [ ] Errors have helpful link attached, see `contributing.md`\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/39221/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/39221/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":7102057359,"node_id":"CE_lADOBC3Cis5NJWvuzwAAAAGnUMuP","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/events/7102057359","actor":{"login":"kodiakhq[bot]","id":49736102,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDk3MzYxMDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/29196?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://a